From 6de933b72efd49d4df1e0ff414422d4311e796c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:45:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1024/1286] Upscale: UniverSR redraws the top of a take or of a
 file made from it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERESY 1024. Post has Upscale. heresy-lab runs UniverSR (ICASSP 2026, MIT,
vendored in vendor/UniverSR, weights in hf_cache/ inside the Kit) in four
modes — Subtle, Normal, High, Extreme: everything above 12, 8, 6 or 4 kHz is
drawn anew — on the take or any file of its tree (a stem, a remaster), in one
or two variants (two noise seeds). By default the original is kept sample for
sample below the cutoff and only the new top is taken, through a smooth
crossover. The model takes mono and about 15 GB for 30 s, so channels go one
by one in 20 s pieces joined by 1 s equal-power crossfades; measured on a
30 s excerpt, the joined render differs from a one-piece render at the join
exactly as much as away from it (1.74 dB against 1.78 dB in 12–24 kHz).
Each run is a branch of the tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
